{% doc %}
  The top of a page: crumb or eyebrow, the H1 sized to its box, deck and call to action (DESIGN.md
  §6.3, §6.6). The same block goes in a hero's title box and in a page header, so every page
  title is written once. The section keeps its own wrapper (.gs-hero__box or .gs-page-head) and
  adds anything after it (an article's date, the search form, the 404 page's ways on).

  An eyebrow that names another page links back to it as a crumb (DS-80, Proposed), unless it is
  this page.

  @param {string} title - The page title, as plain text or a translation. Required
  @param {string} [eyebrow] - The label above the title
  @param {object} [back] - The page the eyebrow names, if any
  @param {string} [deck] - Intro text; line breaks are kept
  @param {object} [cta] - A link field's value, shown as the page's button

  @example
  {%- render 'gs-title-block', title: page.title, eyebrow: eyebrow, back: back, deck: f.intro.value, cta: cta -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- if back.id != blank and back.id != page.id -%}
  <p class="gs-crumb"><a href="{{ back.url }}">{{ eyebrow | escape }}</a></p>
{%- elsif eyebrow != blank -%}
  <p class="gs-eyebrow">{{ eyebrow | escape }}</p>
{%- endif -%}
<h1 class="gs-h1"{% render 'gs-fit', text: title %}>{{ title | escape_once }}</h1>
{%- if deck != blank -%}
  <p class="gs-deck">{{ deck | escape_once | newline_to_br }}</p>
{%- endif -%}
{%- if cta.url != blank -%}
  <div class="gs-actions">{%- render 'gs-link', link: cta, class: 'gs-button' -%}</div>
{%- endif -%}
